From b9c4038a22ca119b09de0f008bbd24edc380d46b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 06:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Ship the licence of the bundled SQLCipher amalgamation

Upstream-Status: To upstream [needs a pull request against coleifer/sqlcipher3; not submitted from this automated port run]

The extension compiles the vendored SQLCipher 4.12.0 amalgamation
(vendor/sqlite3.c, BSD-3-Clause, ZETETIC LLC; CIPHER_VERSION_NUMBER in
the amalgamation matches the 4.12.0 cited by this repo's own
patches/sqlcipher3/0.6.2 licence patch, since this checkout vendors
the same amalgamation) and dynamically links libcrypto from whatever
OpenSSL the build image ships, but the wheel otherwise ships only
sqlcipher3's own LICENSE. Add LICENSE.sqlcipher at the project root,
where setuptools' default license-files glob (LICEN[CS]E*) picks it up
into dist-info/licenses/ with no packaging change. The matching
LICENSE.openssl is added by the workflow at build time instead of by a
patch: unlike the conan-pinned 0.6.2+ build, this (pre-conan) 0.6.0
setup.py links against whichever OpenSSL the manylinux_riscv64 image's
openssl-devel package provides, so its licence is copied from the
image's own package metadata rather than pinned to a version here.
The SQLite core in the amalgamation is public domain and needs no
notice.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.sqlcipher | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.sqlcipher

diff --git a/LICENSE.sqlcipher b/LICENSE.sqlcipher
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3f71443
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.sqlcipher
